 "system_texts": {
  "dint": "The state is an 8-bit flag mask. Apply each action to the state, in order. An action is applicable only if all its pre_on bits are set and all its pre_off bits are clear in the current state; an inapplicable action leaves the state unchanged. For an applicable action, apply delete bits first, then add bits. Return only the final resulting state as a JSON integer. Names and costs do not change the state.",
  "strace": "The state is an 8-bit flag mask. Apply each action to the state, in order. An action is applicable only if all its pre_on bits are set and all its pre_off bits are clear in the current state; an inapplicable action leaves the state unchanged. For an applicable action, apply delete bits first, then add bits. Return only a JSON object with the keys cmp, calc and after, in this order: cmp holds on_miss (the positions of pre_on bits that are clear, bit 0 being the least significant), off_hit (the positions of pre_off bits that are set), viol (how many positions are listed) and ok (true if the action is applicable); calc is the state the action produces; after is the final resulting state as a JSON integer. Names and costs do not change the state.",
  "bbits": "The state is an 8-bit flag mask, written as a string of 8 binary digits with the most significant bit first; pre_on, pre_off, delete and add are written the same way. Apply each action to the state, in order. An action is applicable only if all its pre_on bits are set and all its pre_off bits are clear in the current state; an inapplicable action leaves the state unchanged. For an applicable action, apply delete bits first, then add bits. Return only a JSON object with the keys applicable (true or false) and after (the final resulting state as a string of 8 binary digits), in this order. Names and costs do not change the state.",
  "ffill": "The state is an 8-bit flag mask. Apply each action to the state, in order. An action is applicable only if all its pre_on bits are set and all its pre_off bits are clear in the current state; an inapplicable action leaves the state unchanged. For an applicable action, apply delete bits first, then add bits. Return only a JSON object with the keys fill (a run of dots) and after (the final resulting state as a JSON integer), in this order. Names and costs do not change the state."
 },
